    <subfield code="a">"Thoughts on painting, politics, museums, money, governments, censorship, art criticism, and terrorism are bound into this book with modest little illustrations from the artist's signature source: the dollar bill. In order to read the uncut pages you must peer into the folds, which lends the experience of reading an air of transgression, no doubt desired by this artist in the midst of personal-political confession." Printed Matter.</subfield>
